Chapter 7. Fano and Identification

7.1 The classical Fano inequality

Theorem 7.1 (Fano). Let M be an \mathcal{M}-valued random variable, Y^n an observation, and \hat{M} = \hat{M}(Y^n) an estimator with P_e := P(\hat{M} \neq M). Then

H(M \mid Y^n) \le h(P_e) + P_e \log(|\mathcal{M}| - 1),

where h(p) = -p \log p - (1-p) \log(1-p).

7.2 The data-processing floor

Theorem 7.2 (Data-processing floor). With the Markov chain M \to X \to Y^n,

P_e \ge \frac{H(M) - I(M; X) - 1}{\log(|\mathcal{M}| - 1)}.

Proof. By the data-processing inequality, I(M; Y^n) \le I(M; X). By Fano's inequality,

H(M \mid Y^n) \le h(P_e) + P_e \log(|\mathcal{M}| - 1).

Since I(M; Y^n) = H(M) - H(M \mid Y^n),

I(M; Y^n) \ge H(M) - h(P_e) - P_e \log(|\mathcal{M}| - 1).

Bound h(P_e) \le 1 and I(M; Y^n) \le I(M; X), then rearrange. \square

Remark 7.3. The inequality I(M; Y^n) \le h(P_e) + P_e \log(|\mathcal{M}| - 1) has the wrong direction and is not a valid Fano bound. This error appeared in Version 0.3 and is corrected here.

7.3 Adaptive candidate pools

Theorem 7.4 (Adaptive Fano, conditional form). Let K \ge 2 be the random size of an adaptively constructed candidate pool, and let M be uniform over the pool given K. Then for any estimator,

P_e(k) \ge \frac{H(M \mid K = k) - I(M; Y^n \mid K = k) - 1}{\log(k - 1)}.

Averaging over K,

\bar{P}_e \ge \mathbb{E}_K \left[ \frac{H(M \mid K) - 1}{\log(K - 1)} \right].

Proof. Condition on K = k, apply Theorem 7.1 within the stratum, average over K. \square

Remark 7.5. The bound H(M \mid K) - \log K - 1 appearing in Version 0.3 is vacuous when M is uniform: H(M \mid K) = \log K makes the numerator non-positive. The correct numerator is H(M \mid K) - 1.

7.4 Fano is not a certification bound

Remark 7.6. Fano's inequality constrains identification — the recovery of M from Y^n. It does not constrain certification — the binary decision of descent with a witness. For certification, the correct bound is the Le Cam minimax bound of Chapter 6.

